From: TicWatch Pro 5 (dace) port
Subject: [PATCH] tty: msm_geni_serial: force FIFO on the BT HS UART

The QUP wrapper @4ac0000 has no IOMMU domain (it is built-in and apps-smmu is a
module; of_iommu_configure() is not retried) and the HS UART SE-DMA takes an
RX_SBE (bus error) on the first open() -> hard SoC reset. With gsi_mode=0 and
FIFO NOT disabled, we force GENI_SE_FIFO for the non-console HS UART (the BT):
it uses CPU PIO, no DMA, and avoids the bus error. dace bring-up patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [dace bring-up]
---
diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c
index 0d32f2595297..3ccbc40b9e37 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/msm_geni_serial.c
@@ -37,6 +37,16 @@
 
 static bool con_enabled = IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SERIAL_MSM_GENI_CONSOLE_DEFAULT_ENABLED);
 
+/*
+ * dace (TicWatch Pro 5): force FIFO on the HS UART. The QUP wrapper has no
+ * IOMMU domain (it is built-in and apps-smmu is a module) and its SE-DMA takes
+ * an RX_SBE (bus error) on open -> hard reset. FIFO uses CPU PIO (no DMA) and
+ * avoids the problem. It only affects the non-console HS UART (the BT).
+ */
+static bool dace_hs_uart_fifo = true;
+module_param(dace_hs_uart_fifo, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(dace_hs_uart_fifo, "Force FIFO mode for HS UART (avoid QUP SE-DMA)");
+
 /* UART specific GENI registers */
 #define SE_UART_LOOPBACK_CFG		(0x22C)
 #define SE_GENI_CFG_REG80		(0x240)
@@ -3573,7 +3583,7 @@ static int msm_geni_serial_port_setup(struct uart_port *uport)
 	geni_write_reg(rxstale, uport->membase, SE_UART_RX_STALE_CNT);
 	if (msm_port->gsi_mode) {
 		msm_port->xfer_mode = GENI_GPI_DMA;
-	} else if (!uart_console(uport)) {
+	} else if (!uart_console(uport) && !dace_hs_uart_fifo) {
 		/* For now only assume FIFO mode. */
 		msm_port->xfer_mode = GENI_SE_DMA;
 		/* TX packing */
